---
orbit 2026
component SiteHeader
props {
  shop: Shop
  menu: List<MenuItem>
}
settings {
  showSearch: Toggle = true label "Show search"
  sticky: Toggle = true label "Sticky header"
}
---
{# PORT NOTE (header): THE central finding. Three things here cannot be
   expressed, and all three are interactivity:

   1. The mobile nav toggle. The original is a useState drawer. Below it is a
      <details>/<summary> disclosure, which needs no script and works — but it
      is a different interaction (no focus trap, no scroll lock, no animation).
   2. Live search. The original fetches suggestions as you type. Below it is a
      plain GET form to /search. Correct, and a real downgrade.
   3. The cart flyout and its live count. The original opens a drawer and
      updates the badge without a reload. Below it is a link to /cart, and the
      count is whatever the server rendered.

   None of these is a missing FILTER or a missing type. Each is the same
   missing thing: a way for the theme to say "put the platform's cart drawer
   here". That is one mechanism, not three, and it is what E0/E1 proposes. #}
<header class="hdr hdr--sticky-{settings.sticky}">
  <nav class="hdr__nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <a class="hdr__logo" href="/">
      <img src={imgUrl(shop.logo, 160, format: "webp")} alt={shop.name} width="160" height="40"/>
    </a>
    {# The mobile menu: a disclosure, because no author-written JS exists. #}
    <details class="hdr__menu">
      <summary class="hdr__menu-button" aria-label="Menu">Menu</summary>
      <ul class="hdr__links">
        <for item of={menu}>
          <li>
            <a href={item.url} aria-current?={item.current}>{item.label}</a>
          </li>
        </for>
      </ul>
    </details>
    <div class="hdr__actions">
      <if {settings.showSearch}>
        <form class="hdr__search" action={shop.searchUrl} method="get" role="search">
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="q">Search</label>
          <input id="q" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Search" autocomplete="off"/>
          <button type="submit">Search</button>
        </form>
      </if>
      <a class="hdr__account" href={shop.accountUrl}>Account</a>
      <a class="hdr__cart" href={shop.cartUrl}>
        Cart 
        <if {shop.cartCount > 0}><span class="hdr__cart-count">{shop.cartCount}</span></if>
      </a>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>
